-- METRIC-PLAYBOOKS-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000266, BREACH-DOCTOR-1 family METRIC). Owner, 2026-10-24 and 2026-10-26: "FLEET IS NOT SELF-DIAGNOSING ITS OWN BREACHES AND AUTOMATICALLY REMEDIATING".
-- The doctor engine (qnfo-fleet-control breachDoctorTick, migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor.sql) ships with four CODE-MERGE/CODE-LOOP playbooks, so its first ticks classified the METRIC-TRIGGER-*, METRIC-REGRESSION-1
-- and METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 family (87 open issues on 2026-10-26 11:20Z) as unclassified. This file adds the playbooks for the parts of that family a rule can prove from ids, counts and enum codes,
-- on top of BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1/2/3 (operator words normalised by two D1 triggers, duplicate and contradicted triggers disabled, breach_causes): it builds only what those left, and every rule was
-- re-measured on live qnfo-audit before it was written (SELECT only, 2026-10-26 11:30Z, trigger_sql as the engine runs it).
--   MD-1  duplicate open issue per trigger id          0 hits live (recurs: triggers 354, 409 and 8888 in one week), supersede to the survivor
--   MD-4  recovered but open                           0 hits live (second path of TRIGGER-RECOVERY-1), close with the reading and the streak length
--   MD-6  covered by the parent metric                 4 hits live, 6 once the file has raised the parents (4 reachable by the doctor), supersede the child of a disabled duplicate trigger to the parent's open issue
--   MD-7  time-gated 24 h heartbeat metric             3 hits live (2875, 99936, 2861), dated disposition from a replay of the fleet_tick gap
-- WHAT A REPLAY OF THE AUDIT FOUND ALREADY DONE OR WRONG (so it is not built; the reasons are the evidence):
--   MD-2 (operator outside the evaluator set): 0 enabled triggers have one; BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 normalises '>' '>=' '<' '<=' '=' '==' on insert and update (two D1 triggers) and the view reads them.
--   MD-5 (blind metric): the registry already says UNMEASURED for the one blind breach issue (1838, trigger 413); the other NULL readings are metrics with no issue.
--   MD-9 (close deadlock): the contract of issue 2323 passes exactly when the improvement loop's latest state_json no longer lists the finding and the loop still lists it, so the fail verdict is true and not a
--     deadlock; the four METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 contracts are 'deferred' and do not block a close (issue_close_evidence_required only refuses fail, vacuous-probe-result, probe-error and the two probe refusals).
--     Superseding a correct probe to close a live finding would be the move CLOSE-BINDS-TO-PROBE-1 exists to stop. The cause of those issues is the loop judging its own output (MD-8), which is code: MD-P2 below.
--   MD-3, MD-8, MD-10, MD-11, MD-12, MD-13, MD-14 are decisions or code levers (a replay of the sitemap, a statistical rule, a lever library, definition migrations): not playbooks. MD-P1a/b/c, MD-P2 and
--     MD-P4 below are the code and design levers the audit names with a unique anchor, filed as agent_issues rows with a doer and an outcome probe.
-- ENGINE: one const line of qnfo-fleet-control (BD_WRITE_TABLES gains metric_dispositions, the table MD-7 writes; 0.53.1). metric_registry and analytics_metric_triggers are NOT added: no rule here writes them.
-- Every statement of a rule binds the one issue by a top-level id = ?1 (BREACH-DOCTOR-FIX-1, 0.53.0), so MD-6 cannot raise its parent issue: it supersedes into a parent that is already at least as urgent, and this file
-- raises today's parents once (99938 to critical, 100301 to high: the urgency their children carried), with the previous priorities kept in bak_20261026_metric_playbooks_priority for the Rollback.
-- NEW TABLES: metric_deps (child metric -> the metric that keeps its meaning, relation names the replay) and metric_dispositions (a dated, released-or-expiring record that a breach is time-gated). Neither holds
--   work: a disposition is a reason with an expiry (ANTIFRAGILE-1) and fm-metric-disposition-expired reads it; the issue it describes stays open.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE breach_playbooks SET enabled = 0, mode = 'measure' WHERE rule_id IN ('MD-1', 'MD-4', 'MD-6', 'MD-7'); UPDATE metric_deps SET active = 0; UPDATE agent_issues SET priority = (SELECT b.priority FROM bak_20261026_metric_playbooks_priority b WHERE b.id = agent_issues.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261026_metric_playbooks_priority); UPDATE metric_dispositions SET released_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE released_at IS NULL; UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'open', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE status = 'closed' AND id IN (SELECT issue_id FROM issue_triage WHERE rc = 'breach-doctor:MD-6:migration'); UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = 'triaged', close_evidence = NULL WHERE rc = 'breach-doctor:MD-6:migration'
-- spof-review: no cron, worker or binding; four playbook rows and two small tables on the existing doctor tick. The doctor's second path is the qnfo-cloud-ops watch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1), which files an issue when the doctor tick stalls.
-- charter-pillar: autonomy. Table family +2 (metric_deps, metric_dispositions), funded by the retirement issue BREACH-DOCTOR-RETIRE-1.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS metric_deps (
  child_metric TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  parent_metric TEXT NOT NULL,
  relation TEXT NOT NULL,
  note TEXT,
  active INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'))
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS metric_dispositions (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  metric TEXT NOT NULL,
  kind TEXT NOT NULL,
  issue_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
  trigger_id INTEGER,
  expires_at TEXT NOT NULL,
  evidence TEXT NOT NULL,
  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  released_at TEXT
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_metric_dispositions_issue ON metric_dispositions (issue_id, kind, released_at);

-- relation disabled-duplicate: BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 (2026-10-26) disabled the child trigger and its note names the metric that keeps the meaning (read from analytics_metric_triggers.notes on live D1);
-- relation window-of-fleet-tick: the metric is the share of a 24 h window of fleet_tick slots, so one closed gap in the heartbeat explains it until the gap leaves the window (MD-7).
